.TH GSTRADIO 1 "November 2026" "gstradio 0.5" "Icecast media streaming system"
.SH NAME
gstradio \- stream MP3 audio to an icecast server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gstradio
[\fB\-BVv\fR]
[\fB\-T\fR [\fIformat\fR]]
[\fB\-c\fR \fIconfigfile\fR]
[\fB\-D\fR \fIbasedir\fR]
[\fB\-S builtin\fR [\fB\-F\fR \fIplaylist\fR] [\fB\-r\fR] | \fB\-S python\fR|\fBperl\fR [\fB\-M\fR \fImodule\fR]]
[\fB\-C\fR \fIcrossfadesecs\fR]
[[\fB\-m\fR \fImount\fR] [\fB\-h\fR \fIhost\fR] [\fB\-p\fR \fIport\fR] [\fB\-P\fR \fIpassword\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fIprotocol\fR] [\fB\-n\fR \fIname\fR] [\fB\-g\fR \fIgenre\fR] [\fB\-d\fR \fIdescription\fR]
[\fB\-u\fR \fIurl\fR] [\fB\-s\fR] [\fB\-b\fR \fIbitrate\fR] [\fB\-f\fR \fIdumpfile\fR]
[\fB\-R\fR [\fB\-H\fR \fIsamplerate\fR] [\fB\-N\fR \fIchannels\fR]]] ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gstradio
is a source client for icecast servers built on GStreamer. It is derived
from IceS 0.4, whose command line options it shares. Its features include:
.IP \(bu 2
A scripting interface to its playlist engine, using python or perl, in
addition to a builtin static playlist.
.IP \(bu
Reading source audio from a FIFO or standard input.
.IP \(bu
On-the-fly reencoding of the source audio to a different bitrate, number of
channels and/or sample rate. Ogg Vorbis and FLAC files (and anything else
GStreamer can decode) are transcoded to MP3.
.IP \(bu
Crossfading between tracks (requires reencoding on every stream).
.IP \(bu
Multiple streams from the same playlist, e.g. for broadband and narrowband
listeners at the same time.
.IP \(bu
A constantly updated cue file describing the current track.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Execution options"
.TP
.B \-B
Detach from the console and run in the background. The process id is
written to \fIbasedir\fR/gstradio.pid.
.TP
.BI \-c " configfile"
Load configuration from \fIconfigfile\fR instead of the default
(\fBgstradio.conf\fR in the current directory or the system configuration
directory). Command line options override the file.
.TP
.BI \-D " basedir"
Write the log, cue and pid files to \fIbasedir\fR (default /tmp).
.TP
.BR \-T " [" \fIformat\fR ]
Prefix each line logged to standard output with a timestamp formatted by
\fBstrftime\fR(3). If \fIformat\fR is omitted, \fB%c\fR is used. Disabled
by default.
.TP
.B \-V
Show version information and compile-time options and exit.
.TP
.B \-v
Run in verbose mode.
.SS "Playlist options"
.TP
.BI \-S " interpreter"
Playlist handler: \fBbuiltin\fR (default), \fBpython\fR or \fBperl\fR.
.TP
.BI \-F " playlist"
For the builtin handler, the playlist file: one audio file path per line
(default playlist.txt). Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
The file is re-read when it changes. A line consisting of \fB\-\fR reads
audio from standard input.
.TP
.B \-r
Play the builtin playlist in random order.
.TP
.BI \-M " module"
Python or perl module to load instead of the default, \fBgstradio\fR.
.TP
.BI \-C " crossfadesecs"
Crossfade between tracks for \fIcrossfadesecs\fR seconds. Tracks shorter
than 10 seconds or twice the fade length are not faded into.
.SS "Stream options"
.TP
.BI \-m " mount"
Create a stream at mountpoint \fImount\fR. May be given several times to
create multiple streams from the same playlist; the stream options that
follow apply to that mount only. The default mount is /gstradio.
.TP
.BI \-h " host"
Icecast server host (default 127.0.0.1).
.TP
.BI \-p " port"
Icecast server port (default 8000). With the icy protocol, libshout
connects to \fIport\fR+1, as Shoutcast servers expect.
.TP
.BI \-P " password"
Source password (default letmein).
.TP
.BI \-t " protocol"
\fBhttp\fR (icecast 2, default), \fBxaudiocast\fR (icecast 1) or
\fBicy\fR (shoutcast).
.TP
.B \-i
Same as \fB\-t icy\fR.
.TP
.BI \-n " name"
Stream name.
.TP
.BI \-g " genre"
Stream genre.
.TP
.BI \-d " description"
Stream description.
.TP
.BI \-u " url"
Stream URL.
.TP
.B \-s
Do not mark the stream as public (no directory listing).
.TP
.BI \-b " bitrate"
Stream bitrate in kbps (default 128). Unless reencoding, this is only
informational.
.TP
.BI \-f " dumpfile"
Ask the server to dump the stream to \fIdumpfile\fR (xaudiocast only).
.TP
.B \-R
Reencode this stream at the bitrate given with \fB\-b\fR. MP3 files that
already match the stream's bitrate, sample rate and channels are passed
through unchanged. Required for Ogg Vorbis and FLAC input.
.TP
.BI \-H " samplerate"
Output sample rate when reencoding. By default LAME's choice for the
bitrate is used.
.TP
.BI \-N " channels"
Output channels when reencoding: 1 (mono) or 2 (stereo).
.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
An XML document whose root is \fBConfiguration\fR in the namespace
\fBhttps://github.com/danengholm/gstradio\fR, containing:
.TP
.B Playlist
\fBFile\fR, \fBRandomize\fR, \fBType\fR, \fBModule\fR, \fBCrossfade\fR.
.TP
.B Execution
\fBBackground\fR, \fBVerbose\fR, \fBBaseDirectory\fR, \fBTimestamp\fR.
.TP
.B Stream
(repeatable) \fBServer\fR (\fBHostname\fR, \fBPort\fR, \fBPassword\fR,
\fBProtocol\fR), \fBMountpoint\fR, \fBDumpfile\fR, \fBName\fR,
\fBGenre\fR, \fBDescription\fR, \fBURL\fR, \fBPublic\fR, \fBBitrate\fR,
\fBReencode\fR, \fBSamplerate\fR, \fBChannels\fR.
.PP
See gstradio.conf.dist for an annotated example.
.SH PLAYLIST SCRIPTING
A python (3) or perl module may define these functions:
.TP
.B gstradio_init
Called once at startup. A negative result makes gstradio exit.
.TP
.B gstradio_shutdown
Called before gstradio exits.
.TP
.B gstradio_get_next
Called at each track change; returns the path of the next file to play. An
empty result ends streaming. This function is required.
.TP
.B gstradio_get_metadata
Called after \fBgstradio_get_next\fR. If it returns a string, it is used as the
streamed title instead of one built from the file's tags or name.
.TP
.B gstradio_get_lineno
Called after \fBgstradio_get_next\fR; the returned number is written to the cue
file.
.PP
Modules are searched for in the playlist module directory and
the current directory (plus PYTHONPATH for python). Perl modules must end
with "1;".
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Clean shutdown.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Close and reopen the log file and reload the playlist (or restart the
playlist script).
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Skip to the next track immediately.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I basedir/gstradio.log
Log file.
.TP
.I basedir/gstradio.cue
Current track: file name, size, bitrate, length (d:h:m:s), percent played,
playlist line, artist and title, one per line.
.TP
.I basedir/gstradio.pid
Process id when running in the background.
.TP
.I sysconfdir/gstradio.conf
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I moduledir/gstradio.py, moduledir/gstradio.pm
Default playlist modules.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on a normal shutdown (signal or end of playlist), 1 on error, including
more than 10 consecutive unplayable tracks or more than 10 consecutive
errors on a stream.
.SH AUTHORS
IceS was originally written by Alexander Hav\(:ang and maintained by
Brendan Cully. gstradio is a GStreamer-based reimplementation of IceS 0.4.
